@YinghaoXu1 & Jian Gao built LingBot-Map, a 3D model that reconstructs live scenes from video streams at ~20 FPS, stable over 10,000+ frames, without drift. 

Instead of engineering a classical SLAM pipeline, they encoded SLAM's logic directly into a transformer. three memory types (coordinate grounding, local geometry, drift correction) in one unified attention mechanism. Open weights, deployable, and the repo is already getting updates this week.

